## Follow-up residual (NOT closed this turn)

- **B6 — CRIT: trace the 22× / 725× blow-up.** Cause not yet attributed. Likely `tc_call_ret.oo` or `c_emit_helpers.oo:235-236` ABI signature verification on the new call site.
- **B7 — HIGH: bound the regression.** Three owner choices: (a) revert `env.oo:6` (re-introduces latent stack-overflow); (b) keep the fix and tune the type-checker (bounds the cost); (c) keep the fix and document the cost (treat as known tail).
- **B8 — GATE: F26 harness threshold recalibration.** 24 GiB threshold was set when peak was 22.8 GB; new peak is 28.3 GB.
- **B9 — GATE: `p7_check_main_smoke.oo` should record peak RSS + ELF build ID** (already in B4/SPRINT).
- **B10 — MED: emit-c fail-closed** — verify DE3 single-call emit path before any revert.

## Lane ownership

- DE1/DE2/DE3: wall profile, RSS pattern, emit inspection.
- PV1/PV2: repro stats, revert test.
- MEM: bound analysis.
- INT: build idempotency.
- SEC: new surface.
- HARN/HYG: harness coverage, line lock.
- DOCS: this synthesis.
- COORD: pending rollup once per-agent findings land.

## What is NOT claimed

- The 22× / 725× numbers are 04:00 snapshot, not final.
- The cause is **not** attributed yet — three plausible sites (`tc_call_ret.oo`, `c_emit_helpers.oo`, `token_fmt.oo`).
- No claim that the fix is wrong — the latent DoS was real; the cost is a type-checker depth problem.
- No claim that revert is safe — re-introduces the stack-overflow.

